---
import Layout from "@components/Layout.astro";
import PageHeader from "@components/PageHeader.astro";
import { Grid, Card, Badge } from "webcoreui/astro";
import DeckSection from "@components/DeckSection.astro";
import DecklistTooltip from "@components/DecklistTooltip.astro";
import CopyDeckButton from "@components/CopyDeckButton.astro";
import { modernDecklists, getCopyString } from "@data/decklists";
---

<Layout
    title="Tournament Lists - Replenish Guide"
    description="Browse the most successful and innovative Replenish decklists in MTG Premodern. Easily copy configurations directly to MTGO, from stock builds to experimental control shells."
>
    <PageHeader
        title="Tournament Lists"
        description="Explore competitive championship configurations of Parallax Replenish—from standard tournament frameworks to innovative creatureless architectures."
        imageSrc="/src/assets/banners/opalescence.jpeg"
        imageAlt="Opalescence"
        imageCaption="Opalescence by John Avon"
        isCard={true}
    />

    <Card title="Architectural Philosophies" titleTag="h2">
        <p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
            While every successful Replenish list relies on an invariant engine core, competitive pilots adopt markedly different high-level philosophies when tailoring their 75 for regional championship metas:
        </p>
        <ul style="padding-left: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0;">
            <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                <strong>Game 1 Interference vs. Blanking Removal:</strong> Bryan Gulotta’s NA Championship build positions four copies of <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Meddling Mage">Meddling Mage</a> directly in the maindeck—securing immediate proactive interference against combo and permission-heavy control. In contrast, classical frameworks like Brian Siu’s and Alessandro Galli’s retain zero creatures in the maindeck, systematically blanking the opponent's Game 1 spot removal.
            </li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                <strong>Transformational vs. Pure Control Sideboards:</strong> While traditional configurations pivot aggressively post-board into midrange threat structures (<a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Exalted Angel">Exalted Angel</a>), innovative experimental builds like MarineBiomancer’s "Creatureless 75" abandon creature transitions entirely. By fielding zero creatures across all 75 slots, they permanently render opposing spot removal and sideboard creature sweepers inert.
            </li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 0;">
                <strong>Metagame Flex-Slot Tailoring:</strong> Because the foundational combo engine requires approximately 52 invariant slots, pilots freely modulate flex allocations of <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Decree of Silence">Decree of Silence</a>, <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Tsabo's Web">Tsabo's Web</a>, and <a href="#" class="card-hover" data-card-name="Seal of Cleansing">Seal of Cleansing</a> to match anticipated regional target densities (refer to our detailed <a href="/analysis" style="color: var(--w-color-info); text-decoration: underline; font-weight: bold;">Maindeck Analysis</a> for quantitative flex slot guidance).
            </li>
        </ul>
    </Card>

    <div
        style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 3rem; margin-top: 2rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;"
    >
        {
            modernDecklists.map((deck) => (
                <Card>
                    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                        <h2 style="margin: 0; font-size: 1.5rem;">
                            {deck.player}
                        </h2>
                        <CopyDeckButton decklist={getCopyString(deck)} />
                    </div>
                    {deck.badgeText && (
                        <div style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                            <Badge
                                theme="secondary"
                                small={true}
                            >
                                {deck.badgeText}
                            </Badge>
                        </div>
                    )}
                    {deck.description && (
                        <p
                            style="margin-bottom: 2rem; padding: 1rem; background-color: var(--w-color-primary-95); border-radius: var(--w-lg-radius); border-left: 4px solid var(--w-color-primary);"
                            set:html={deck.description}
                        />
                    )}

                    <Grid column={3} gap="lg">
                        {deck.columns.map((col) => (
                            <div>
                                {col.sections.map((sec) => (
                                    <DeckSection
                                        title={sec.title}
                                        items={sec.items}
                                    />
                                ))}
                            </div>
                        ))}
                    </Grid>
                </Card>
            ))
        }
    </div>
    <DecklistTooltip />
</Layout>
